[?25l[0m[38;5;141m> [0mThe translation is correct. One real mismatch was found and fixed.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe bug: SIGPIPE.[22m The Rust runtime sets [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m to [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m, so a write to a closed pipe returned [38;5;10mEPIPE[0m instead of killing the process. Since the translation ignores write errors (as C's unchecked [38;5;10mprintf[0m does), the Rust program ran to completion and exited 0 where the C program was killed by signal 13. Both stdout and stderr were empty in each case, so this was invisible to any check that didn't compare exit status. Fixed with [38;5;10msignal(SIGPIPE, SIG_DFL)[0m as the first statement of [38;5;10mmain[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mWhat the C branches on[22m, all covered: [38;5;10mfgets[0m returning NULL only on immediate EOF; [38;5;10mdata == 0[0m; every length in [38;5;10m0..=99[0m; [38;5;10mdata >= 100[0m skipping the copy so [38;5;10mdest[0m stays empty; and negative [38;5;10mdata[0m, where the length sign-extends to a near-[38;5;10mSIZE_MAX[0m [38;5;10msize_t[0m and [38;5;10mstrncpy[0m runs off the 100-byte buffer, killing the process with SIGSEGV. No negative value escapes that fault.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Three non-obvious behaviors the existing translation already got right, and which I verified rather than changed:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- On empty stdin the C prints [38;5;10mfgets() failed.[0m and [3mthen[23m faults — but with stdout on a pipe it is fully buffered, so the message dies in the buffer and observable stdout is empty. Confirmed both directions: nothing under a pipe, [38;5;10mfgets() failed.\r\n[0m under a pty.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10matoi[0m is [38;5;10m(int) strtol(...)[0m, so it saturates at [38;5;10mLONG_MAX[0m [3mbefore[23m truncating to 32 bits. [38;5;10m2147483648[0m becomes [38;5;10mINT_MIN[0m and faults; [38;5;10m4294967396[0m becomes [38;5;10m100[0m and prints an empty line.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mfgets(buf, 14, ...)[0m reads at most 13 bytes and never past the newline, so long first lines are truncated to a different value and trailing lines are ignored.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mVerification:[22m [38;5;10mtranslation/tests/differential.rs[0m — 18 tests, no [38;5;10m#[ignore][0m, driving both built executables as subprocesses and comparing stdout, stderr and exit status (including signal). [38;5;10mcargo test[0m passes in both profiles. Independently, an external fuzz of 8,488 inputs over a byte alphabet including NUL, CR, VT, FF and [38;5;10m0xff[0m produced zero mismatches. [38;5;10mc_src[0m checksums are unchanged. Findings are recorded in [38;5;10mtranslation/ERRORS.md[0m.[0m[0m
